 "q-10902" :question/id #uuid "f57e3668-6559-58e3-8b4a-23bfd386a16c" :question/math-academy-id "q-10902" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x)$ for $f(x)={x}^{6}+{x}^{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{6}+{x}^{5})}^{′} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {x}^{5}+5\\cdot {x}^{4} \\\\  & =6{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & ={(6{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4})}^{′} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 6{x}^{4}+4\\cdot 5{x}^{3} \\\\  & =30{x}^{4}+20{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-10902/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10902"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-28556/selection/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" :answer/id #uuid "d0eac07d-22da-5e4a-bbeb-ac208ac00a6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28556/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "1909bd0d-7c92-554a-85e1-6ffc1df4f17b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28556/selection/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" :answer/id #uuid "74f45517-793a-55c0-992b-ada83f6515b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28556/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "3f7564e8-b5bc-549b-bb71-af16e4f99e5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28556/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "7ee1662d-dea8-5d01-89c3-48c180a6f121" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28556/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c7844d1-132c-5cc2-9c73-53aa1ae43ba0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-28556/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-28556/selection/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" "q-28556/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" "q-28556/selection/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" "q-28556/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" "q-28556/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-28556" :question/id #uuid "2228ba5b-177e-5571-a1af-ea713584740f" :question/math-academy-id "q-28556" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find ${g}^{″}(4)$ if $g(x)=4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}-2x+7.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & ={(4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}-2x+7)}^{′} \\\\  & ={(4{x}^{5/2}-2x+7)}^{′} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{5}{2}){x}^{3/2}-2+0 \\\\  & =10{x}^{3/2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(x) & ={(10{x}^{3/2}-2)}^{′} \\\\  & =10(\\frac{3}{2}){x}^{1/2}-0 \\\\  & =15{x}^{1/2} \\\\  & =15\\sqrt{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=4$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(4) & =15\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =15(2) \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-28556/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-28556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342851/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "56922837-6471-5037-b596-ee75655a6e1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342851/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f626f2e-3d66-5e46-8c01-28c22c432e35" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342851/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-342851/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342851" :question/id #uuid "89d72708-85f3-50d8-be7c-f6b79aaead58" :question/math-academy-id "q-342851" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find ${g}^{″}(1)$ if $g(x)=-{x}^{3}+4x\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n${g}^{″}(1)=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & ={(-{x}^{3}+4x\\sqrt{x})}^{′} \\\\  & ={(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{3/2})}^{′} \\\\  & =3(-{x}^{2})+\\frac{3}{2}(4{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}+6{x}^{1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(x) & ={(-3{x}^{2}+6{x}^{1/2})}^{′} \\\\  & =2(-3x)+\\frac{1}{2}(6{x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =-6x+3{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =-6x+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(1) & =-6(1)+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =-6+3 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-342851/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342851"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10883/selection/abdae52395c6fdcfe9135c6bda6a50910059c16b595eaff0a484739368d34dac" :answer/id #uuid "aa955f6e-beed-5e45-907f-41c258228ba2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/i